# pdf-to-video-ai

Generate narrated Full HD videos from scholarship documents (PDF, DOCX, HTML, TXT) with full provenance tracking.

## Quick Start

```bash
# Linux / macOS
python3 -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli generar /ruta/a/beca --salida salidas/

# Windows
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli generar C:\ruta\a\beca --salida salidas\
```

---

## Installation

### System Dependencies (one-time)

#### Ubuntu / Debian
```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y \
    python3 python3-venv python3-pip \
    ffmpeg libreoffice \
    poppler-utils
```

> **Note**: OCR is handled by PaddleOCR (Python-based) via `pip install -r requirements-ocr.txt`. No system-level tesseract-ocr package is needed.
```

#### Windows (using Chocolatey)
```powershell
# Run PowerShell as Administrator
choco install python ffmpeg libreoffice poppler
```

#### Windows (using Scoop)
```powershell
scoop install python ffmpeg libreoffice poppler
```

#### Windows (manual)
1. **Python**: Download from https://python.org/downloads
2. **ffmpeg**: Download from https://ffmpeg.org/download.html → add to PATH
3. **LibreOffice**: Download from https://libreoffice.org/download
4. **Poppler**: Download from https://github.com/oschwartz10612/poppler-windows/releases

---

## Python Virtual Environment

### Linux / macOS (one-time setup)

```bash
# 1. Create virtual environment (ONLY FIRST TIME)
python3 -m venv .venv

# 2. Activate environment (EVERY TIME YOU USE THE PROGRAM)
source .venv/bin/activate

# 3. Upgrade pip (ONLY FIRST TIME)
pip install --upgrade pip

# 4. Install dependencies (ONLY FIRST TIME)
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 5. (Optional) Install OCR dependencies if needed (for scanned PDFs/images)
pip install -r requirements-ocr.txt
```

### Windows (one-time setup)

```powershell
# 1. Create virtual environment (ONLY FIRST TIME)
python -m venv .venv

# 2. Activate environment (EVERY TIME YOU USE THE PROGRAM)
.venv\Scripts\activate

# 3. Upgrade pip (ONLY FIRST TIME)
python -m pip install --upgrade pip

# 4. Install dependencies (ONLY FIRST TIME)
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 5. (Optional) Install OCR dependencies if needed (for scanned PDFs/images)
pip install -r requirements-ocr.txt
```

---

## Usage

### Every time you want to run the program:

#### Linux / macOS
```bash
# Activate environment (REQUIRED EVERY TIME)
source .venv/bin/activate

# Run single scholarship
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli generar /01-International-Scholarship-Yale-Jackson-School-of-Global-Affairs–MPP/ --salida salidas/

# Batch process all scholarships in a directory
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli lote /ruta/raiz/becas --salida salidas/

# Validate content only
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli validar /ruta/a/beca

# Show version
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli version

# Deactivate when done (OPTIONAL)
deactivate
```

#### Windows
```powershell
# Activate environment (REQUIRED EVERY TIME)
.venv\Scripts\activate

# Run single scholarship
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli generar C:\ruta\a\beca --salida salidas\

# Batch process all scholarships in a directory
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli lote C:\ruta\raiz\becas --salida salidas\

# Validate content only
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli validar C:\ruta\a\beca

# Show version
python -m pdf_to_video_ai.cli version

# Deactivate when done (OPTIONAL)
deactivate
```

---

## Output Structure

For each scholarship folder, the program generates:

```
salidas/<beca>/
├── document.json              # Canonical document model with provenance
├── markdown_consolidado.md    # Markdown export (compatibility)
├── script.json                # Narrated script blocks with source references
├── script.txt                 # Plain text script
├── slides/
│   └── slide_001.png          # Full HD slides (1080x1920 vertical)
├── audio/
│   └── audio_001.mp3          # TTS audio per block
├── subtitles.srt              # Subtitles with real audio timing
├── validation_report.json     # Content validation (structured)
├── validation_report.txt      # Content validation (human-readable)
├── video_final_vertical.mp4   # 1080x1920 (Reels/Shorts/TikTok)
└── video_final_horizontal.mp4 # 1920x1080 (YouTube/Facebook feed)
```

