## Configuration

Edit `config.yaml` to customize:

```yaml
voz:
  name: "es-ES-ElviraNeural"   # edge-tts voice
  rate: "+0%"                   # speech rate
  volume: "+0dB"                # volume

idioma: "es"                    # narration language
duracion_maxima_seg: 45         # max seconds per block
palabras_por_segundo: 2.8       # for duration estimation

subtitulos:
  enabled: true
  burn_in: false                # burn into video
  estilo: "default"

orientaciones:
  - vertical                    # add "horizontal" for 1920x1080

ocr:
  habilitado: false             # enable OCR for scanned pages
  dpi: 300
  idioma: "es"
```

---

## Configuration

Edit `config.yaml` to customize:

```yaml
voz:
  name: "es-ES-ElviraNeural"   # edge-tts voice
  rate: "+0%"                   # speech rate
  volume: "+0dB"                # volume

idioma: "es"                    # narration language
duracion_maxima_seg: 45         # max seconds per block
palabras_por_segundo: 2.8       # for duration estimation

subtitulos:
  enabled: true
  burn_in: false                # burn into video
  estilo: "default"

orientaciones:
  - vertical                    # add "horizontal" for 1920x1080

ocr:
  habilitado: false             # enable OCR for scanned pages
  dpi: 300
  idioma: "es"

salida:
  codec_video: "libx264"
  codec_audio: "aac"
  bitrate_audio: "192k"
  pix_fmt: "yuv420p"

logs:
  nivel: "INFO"
  formato: "json"

llm:
  enabled: false                # set true to use local LLM
  provider: "ollama"            # "ollama" | "llama-cpp" | "transformers"
  model: "phi3:mini"            # or "llama3.2:3b", "mistral:7b"
  base_url: "http://localhost:11434"
  max_tokens: 500
  temperature: 0.2
```

---

## Local LLM (Optional - for better narration fluency)

The program can use a local LLM to improve script fluency without inventing data. This is **optional** and disabled by default.

### Installation (one-time)

#### Linux / macOS / Windows (WSL2)
```bash
# 1. Install Ollama (run once)
curl -fsSL https://ollama.ai/install.sh | sh

# 2. Start Ollama service (run each session or as system service)
ollama serve &

# 3. Pull a small model (one-time, ~2 GB)
ollama pull phi3:mini

# 4. Enable in config.yaml
llm:
  enabled: true
  provider: "ollama"
  model: "phi3:mini"
  base_url: "http://localhost:11434"
```

#### Windows (native)
```powershell
# 1. Download Ollama from https://ollama.ai/download/windows
# 2. Install and run "Ollama" from Start menu
# 3. In a new terminal:
ollama pull phi3:mini

# 4. Enable in config.yaml (same as above)
```

> **Note**: Ollama runs fully offline after model download. No cloud API keys needed.
> **Recommended models for CPU**: `phi3:mini` (2GB), `llama3.2:3b` (2GB), `gemma2:2b` (1.6GB).
> Larger models like `mistral:7b` (4GB) need more RAM.

